  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of emergency shelter and NFI assistance mitigating the impacts of harsh winter weather for internally displaced people, returnees and non-displaced people</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtMedair proposes a localised and&#xa0;integrated approach, through direct implementation and a trusted local partner, to meet the winter needs of&#xa0;displaced and non-displaced conflict-affected individuals in targeted hromadas in Sumska, Kharkivska and&#xa0;Donestka oblasts. It provides last-mile delivery of critical humanitarian winterisation assistance to hard-to-reach areas closest to the frontline in Kharkiv and Donetsk oblasts (within 30km) and Russian border in Sumy oblast (20km) to ensure the most vulnerable&#xa0;people can stay warm through another winter. The activities include provision of insulation and distribution of solid fuel (in cash and in kind)&#xa0;and winter non food items. The winter non food items will be distributed through the local partner Unity  Strength in Kharkiv and Donetsk Oblasts. The partnership&#xa0;is&#xa0;meaningful in terms of budget, duty of care, capacity building and mutual learning.&#xa0;In all activities gender and age consideration, disability inclusion,&#xa0;protection and accountability is mainstreamed.lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
